# bmcd is a cargo package: Buildroot fetches the GitHub archive, runs
# `cargo vendor`, and stores the re-packed archive (the "-cargo2" suffix)
# -- so the sum covers the vendored crates too, exactly as Buildroot does
# for its own cargo packages.
#
# THE SUM DEPENDS ON THE RUST TOOLCHAIN, not just on the commit. The
# archive is named after the commit alone, so a stale one in dl/ looks
# right and hashes wrong. Measured on 2026-09-08 against this very
# commit: rust-bin 1.85.0 vendored
# 9815f9cb190773112439b8979222f45ee79124f15ace2d29c5484141be679f65,
# rust-bin 1.98.1 vendored the sum below. Recompute after any Rust bump,
# from a tree that was re-extracted AFTER the bump -- buildroot_patches/
# are applied at extract time, so a tree extracted before the patch
# changed still carries the old toolchain and will produce the old sum.
#
# The version is commit 9b5cffa on excavador/bmcd branch `hive`, released
# as v2.4.0. Computed with rust-bin 1.98.1 in the pinned container and
# verified by re-running `make bmcd-source` with this file in place.
sha256  84b9825371b085cea0f21ef03efd50893cfb16c0806cecb98c3700d605b44b9c  bmcd-9b5cffa84ee55b468538e1c45af25b379490ba20-cargo2.tar.gz
sha256  809fa1ed21450f59827d1e9aec720bbc4b687434fa22283c6cb5dd82a47ab9c0  LICENSE
